  evaluated it we determined that many  more people died here than elsewhere the  cancer rates in the villages of 15 to 24  times higher than in comparable areas  the irrigation canal in the village is a  stinking cocktail of toxins the sediment  contains heavy metals and many  carcinogenic chemical compounds which  have been washed in by the hue River  farmers abused the contaminated water on  their fields for decades it finally  reached the groundwater and from there  the world's almost all the rivers in  eastern China have become gigantic  sewers for the largest industrial area  in the world thousands of companies pump  toxins into the country's rivers to this  day and the effects are hitting everyone  who lives near the river they're not  limited to factory workers  who and Ison has set up a base for his  campaign to save the hue River in his  home city of shenshu  it's a center for fellow activists he  spent the past decade documenting the  environmental abuses Poole publishes a  blog and state media also carry his  reports he's even won prizes for his  photos in China that helps him finance  his work private donors also support his  efforts but most of the time money is  tight  his sons often help him at work but  things can get quite dicey this mission  would have been life-threatening without  a breathing mask Horace says that only  two weeks after these pictures were  taken and only a little further  downstream farmers went to the river to  get water for their fields there was a  lot of foam when they tried to scoop it  away with their buckets he says but that  released the stink of the contaminated  water they lost consciousness and  collapsed  it was hydrogen sulfide someone called  an ambulance but it was too late it  ended in tragedy with six killed and  four injured together with his eldest  son who all died son has set up eight  observation posts along the river local  helpers even knew as paragliders to  document new sources of pollution when  they find a case who are rings up the  Ministry of the Environment in Beijing  the local authority is early react to  pressure from the top and sometimes the  water quality improves as a result but  it often takes only a few months before  the pollution returns  who as youngest son Minji studies arts  and helps out with the photography he  finds his father's dedication inspiring  and is painting a portrait as a birthday  present  in the past ten years or more of working  to save the hue River  my father has experienced a lot of  injustice contempt and abuse he's been  beaten up and hurt but right from the  start he's fought vigorously for what's  good it's also thanks to him that  awareness of the dangers of water  pollution is growing in China he says he  bit fagor Chasseur so far whoo oh and  his son have visited 400 villages along  the hue river system and documented the  results of the accumulating pollution  today they want to install a water  purification plant in the village of  Duncan song rule they built the water  tank with the villagers years ago a  Chinese man living in Japan saw a report  about who died son and recommended a  microbiological water purifier because  the technology works they're installing  it in village after village sponsored by  supporters in Japan in recent years  we've installed 28 water purification  plants which are providing around 10,000  people with clean water the rates of  cancer have fallen he says in many of  the villages with the equipment there  haven't been any new cancer cases for  five years we've also spoken to the  water and Technology ministries of the  provincial government he says to make  sure they use this technology where it's  needed that's but they haven't given up  hope that their solution might one day  be applied on a greater scale  a lot of people asked me he says why I  let my sons carry out this poorly paid  environmental work they could earn a lot  more money working elsewhere  but I think there are enough people in  our society who earn a lot of money  what's missing are people with a sense  of responsibility I hope that the  younger generation develops a stronger  sense of responsibility compassion and  respect for life the Chinese government  in Beijing is investing the equivalent  of billions of euros a year in economic  development at the same time the  protection of the environment is being  left to individual citizens who often  have access to very limited funds  who are died son has come to Beijing  he's visiting a fundraiser for a  Foundation which seeks to provide clean  drinking water for schoolchildren it  shied away from criticism and in return  it has plenty of coverage in state media  the well-known blogger Deng Fei set up  the foundation he wants to work with who  or die son and try at last to get more  money from the government but first a  prize is awarded to who die son for his  work in saving the ho a river the  organisation's hoped that if they work  together the environmental movement in  China will achieve more  who died son knows that without state  help tighter controls and a stricter  application of the law to polluters his  struggle will achieve very little  but we'll go whenever I'm out in the  country and speaking to people he says I  feel very sad for well bothered I'll  beat you though I don't eat you that's  the reason why I want to change this  tragedy and make the situation better I  have to do something in this life but  I'll only be really happy if I achieve  something who Oh Daesan has waited for  15 years for state recognition and at  last a commission is coming to visit his  clean water project and to speak to  those ill with cancer
 

